{define: CaddG base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 3} 
{define: Emsus4 base-fret 1 frets 0 0 2 0 0 0} 
{define: F base-fret 1 frets x x 3 2 1 1} 
{define: Fm base-fret 1 frets x x 3 1 1 1} 
{define: Gadd base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 3 3} 
{t: IN DREAMS}
{t:  Roy Orbison }
{artist: Roy Orbison }
{composer: Roy Orbison }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MVRunwyoTMA  (Capo 0)

TIP:  The lone (Emsus4) comes after a (Dm) so just move your middle finger up one string while lifting off the other two.  Just add your pinky to the 1st string of the 3rd fret to go from (C) to (CaddG).  Just lift index finger to go form (C) to (Cmaj7).

If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (CaddG) and (Gadd) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  Roy sings the opening verse with just a single strum where the chord appears in brackets.


